/-- The statement of thm:level(qstar), modules/corner/corner.qpp:1007: Let \(n\ge2\), \(N\ge1\) and \(d\ge1\) be counts, \(D=N+d\), and \(f=H+g+f'\) a polynomial in \(n\) variables with rational coefficients, where \(H=\prod_ih_i^{a_i}\) is a form of degree \(N\), with distinct irreducible forms \(h_i\) and counts \(a_i\), \(g\) is a form of degree \(D\), and every term of \(f'\) has degree at least \(D+1\). Put \(V=\{H=0\}\) in the projective space of dimension \(n-1\), \(Z=V\cap\{g=0\}\), \(Z_i\) the points of \(Z\) on \(h_i=0\), \(g_i=\gcd(a_i,d)\), \(\sigma_E=n+Ns\) and \(c'=(n+Ds)/d\), so that \(dc'=\sigma_E+ds\), and write \(c_a\) for \(c'\) at \(d=1\). For a stratum \(\mathcal S\) of \(V\) on which the germ \(H_{\mathcal S}\) of \(H\) has one type let \(Z_{top,\mathcal S}(H;s')\) be the local topological zeta function of that germ, in \(n-1\) variables, and, for a count \(e\), let its layer \(Z^{(e)}_{top,\mathcal S}(H;s')\) be the sum of its terms of \cref{fact:zetatop} over the strata of an embedded resolution of the germ all of whose components have multiplicities divisible by \(e\), so that \(Z^{(1)}_{top,\mathcal S}=Z_{top,\mathcal S}\). With the totient \(J_2\) of Jordan, \(J_2(e)=e^2\prod_\ell(1-\ell^{-2})\) over the primes \(\ell\) dividing \(e\), so that \(\sum_{e\mid m}J_2(e)=m^2\), put, for a germ \(\psi\) of \(H\) at a point, \(\Theta_d(\psi)=\frac1{dc'}+\big(\frac1{\sigma_E}-\frac1{dc'}\big)Z_{top}(\psi;c')-\frac s{(1+s)d}\sum_{e\mid d}J_2(e)Z^{(e)}_{top}(\psi;c')\). The hypothesis \((\mathrm T)\), of transversality, is that no point of \(g=0\) lies on two of the hypersurfaces \(h_i=0\) or is a singular point of one, and that \(g\) cuts each of them transversally. At a prime \(p\) at which the coefficients of \(f\) are \(p\)-integral write \(\#\) for the number of points over \(\mathbb F_p\) of a reduction, put \(T=p^{-s}\), \(X_E=p^{-n}T^N\), \(Y=p^{-n}T^D\) and \(F=(1-T)/(1-p^{-1}T)\), and for a point \(\xi\) of \(V\) over \(\mathbb F_p\), with